Postout for Debian, Ubuntu, and Linux Mint
==========================================

Postout is maintained by DEVOPS CY:

    devops.com.cy


Personal SMTP profiles
----------------------

Run:

    postout config

Personal profiles are stored under:

    ~/.config/postout/profiles.json

These files belong to individual users. Package removal and purge do
not alter configuration inside user home directories.


System SMTP profiles
--------------------

Run:

    postout config --system

Postout requests administrator access and stores shared profiles under:

    /etc/postout/profiles.json

Shared credentials are readable by root and members of the postout
system group. Existing login sessions may need to be restarted after
group membership is added. Alternatively, the user may run:

    newgrp postout


Removal behaviour
-----------------

Ordinary removal preserves shared system configuration:

    sudo apt remove postout

Complete purge removes /etc/postout:

    sudo apt purge postout

Neither operation removes personal profiles from user home directories.
